{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task AGENT-TF-01 is about implementing a Toolformer API-call filtering mechanism. Let me understand the requirements:\n\n1. For each call, compute: `gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n2. Normalize gain by prediction tokens: `normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens`\n3. A call is accepted if:\n   - `parseable == true`\n   - `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n4. Return:\n   - `accepted_call_ids`: list of accepted call IDs in original order\n   - `diagnostics`: list of per-call diagnostics in original order, each with `call_id`, `normalized_gain`, `accepted`\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture:\n\nCase 0, threshold=0.05:\n- call0: gain = 1.94835097 - 0.38569502 = 1.56265595, normalized = 1.56265595/5 = 0.31253119, parseable=true → accepted\n- call1: gain = 1.06116273 - 0.68319969 = 0.37796304, normalized = 0.37796304/4 = 0.09449076, parseable=true → accepted\n- call2: gain = 1.21810502 - 0.47260371 = 0.74550131, normalized = 0.74550131/6 = 0.12425022, parseable=true → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.05721833 - 0.29767903 = 0.7595393, normalized = 0.7595393/5 = 0.1519079 (roughly), parseable=true → accepted\n- call4: gain = 1.06717367 - 0.85733566 = 0.20983801, normalized = 0.20983801/5 = 0.04196760, parseable=true → 0.042 \u003c 0.05 → NOT accepted\n- call5: gain = 1.66191711 - 0.89798497 = 0.76393214, normalized = 0.76393214/4 = 0.190983035, parseable=true → accepted\n\nSo accepted: call0, call1, call2, call3, call5\n\nThe candidate artifact mentions \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - I need to figure out what rounding means. Looking at the schema, `normalized_gain` is type `number`, not integer, so it's a float. The rounding might be to a specific number of decimal places. Let me re-read: \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" This is vague about precision. I'll use standard floating point without explicit rounding, or maybe round to some reasonable decimal places. Actually, looking at the schema it just says `\"type\": \"number\"`, so any float value is fine.\n\nNow let me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be \u003e= 1 for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\n        \n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nWait, the candidate artifact mentions \"rounded per-call diagnostics\". I should round the normalized_gain. But to how many decimal places? Looking at the input values, they have 8 decimal places. Let me think... maybe round to 8 decimal places or just keep full precision. Since the schema says `number`, I'll just return full precision floats. The word \"rounded\" might just mean \"computed/determined\" rather than specifically rounding to certain decimal places.\n\nActually, re-reading: \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics\" - this could mean the diagnostics include rounded (computed) values. I think I'll keep full precision and not round.\n\nAlso, let me make sure I handle validation:\n- Required fields: threshold, calls\n- Each call needs: call_id, loss_without_call, loss_with_call, prediction_tokens, parseable\n- prediction_tokens must be \u003e= 1 (at least one prediction token)\n\nLet me also check case 002 which has a non-parseable call (call4 has parseable=false), so that call should not be accepted regardless of normalized_gain.\n\nFor case 002:\n- call4: loss_without=1.35899862, loss_with=0.11897463, tokens=4, parseable=false\n  - gain = 1.24002399, normalized = 0.310006, but parseable=false → NOT accepted\n\nThe implementation looks correct. Let me finalize it.\n\nNow I need to format this as a JSON response with a single key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string.\n\nLet me write out the complete Python source:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    # Validate required top-level fields\n    if \"threshold\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: threshold\")\n    if \"calls\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: calls\")\n    \n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls must be a list\")\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for i, call in enumerate(calls):\n        # Validate required call fields\n        for field in (\"call_id\", \"loss_without_call\", \"loss_with_call\", \"prediction_tokens\", \"parseable\"):\n            if field not in call:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Call at index {i} missing required field: {field}\")\n        \n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be \u003e= 1 for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\n        \n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain,\n            \"accepted\": accepted\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks good. Now I need to format this as a JSON string properly.\n\nThe response must be:\n```json\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    ...\"}\n```\n\nLet me construct the final JSON response carefully.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate required top-level fields\\n    if \\\"threshold\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required field: threshold\\\")\\n    if \\\"calls\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required field: calls\\\")\\n\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for i, call in enumerate(calls):\\n        # Validate required call fields\\n        for field in (\\\"call_id\\\", \\\"loss_without_call\\\", \\\"loss_with_call\\\", \\\"prediction_tokens\\\", \\\"parseable\\\"):\\n            if field not in call:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Call at index {i} missing required field: {field}\\\")\\n\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        if prediction_tokens \u003c 1:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"prediction_tokens must be \u003e= 1 for call {call_id}\\\")\\n\\n        # Compute gain and normalize by prediction token count\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\\n\\n        # Accept if parseable and normalized gain meets inclusive threshold\\n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted\\n        })\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01gw22R12FgJ1V2IPDJv7cHG","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2484},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2484,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":35,"output_tokens":2217,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1740},"service_tier":"standard"}}